    "note": "**Shore** is the land at the edge of a large area of water, usually a sea or a lake (*the shore of the lake*). **Coast** is used only for the sea and means the whole area of land near it (*a town on the coast*). A **beach** is an area of sand or small stones by the water, where people go to relax or swim. The land at the side of a river is usually its **bank**."
  },
